abstract: "Lean 4 (v4.30.0-rc1) / Mathlib (v4.30.0-rc1) formalization of conditional statements about the Frohmanian tether T(F,G) = -kappa ||omega||^2 int <Pi_u dF, Pi_u dG>, a symmetric quadratic correction to the Arnold Lie-Poisson bracket. The functional derivative is the unique divergence-free L2 gradient along smooth compactly supported test fields (0 where none exists). Proved: symmetry and negative feedback (C3) unconditionally; nondegeneracy of T, polarization of T on functionals with gradients, saturation, projection-dependence and the canonical density of T; canonicity only inside a restricted kernel class (from diagonal saturation and polarization); and an obstruction to damping: every symmetric kernel satisfying (C2) has B(H,M) = 0 for every functional M. (C1) and (C2) for the tether are not proved, and no Jacobi identity is claimed. Refuted in Lean: dH/dw = u, transitivity on Casimir levels, the pointwise strain bound |Du(x)| <= C ||omega||_inf, unrestricted polarization of T, the pointwise weight hypothesis of the canonicity theorem, and Step1Hyp; also removed: TetherIntegralPreserved, a circular Jacobi lemma, an antisymmetric uniqueness clause (vacuous unless T = 0) and a uniform lower bound on local existence times. The Kato local-existence witness asks for the equations only on its own interval. Remaining assumptions are explicit hypotheses: (b) classical results not in Mathlib (Kato local existence, Kato-Beale-Kato-Majda continuation BKMGlobalContinuation, SmoothPhysicalUniqueness, PeriodicBKMContinuation, KatoUniquenessOnExistenceTimes, coadjoint motion of Euler); (d) hypotheses as strong as the open problem (LocalTetherRate, LocalTetherBound, LocalTetherClosingBound, PeriodicTetherClosingBound, PeriodicDirectionDepletionBound, and global-path forms used only by auxiliary lemmas); (c) kernel-class conditions on a competitor kernel in the canonicity theorems; open for T itself: the a.e. weight condition, (C2) at regular vorticities, and (C1). Build: 2726 jobs; 569 theorem constants (514 stated in the sources, 55 auto-generated) and 840 declarations audited; no sorry, no native_decide, no axiom declarations; only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound (enforced in CI). Not a proof of Navier-Stokes global regularity; no Clay Millennium claim."
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Lie-Poisson bracket
  - metriplectic
  - conditional results
